# To enable agent verification of manual facts, uncomment and edit:
# - label: facts configuration
#   id: .config
#   agent: claude
#   batch-size: 10
# Or run: facts config set agent claude

# domain
- a Pulse is a white light launched from one end of the LED strip and moving toward the opposite end @implemented
- the Target Zone is a contiguous yellow region of the LED strip whose brightness follows a Breathing Cycle @implemented
- Progress is represented by Hits shrinking the Target Zone toward its configured minimum and increasing its Breathing Rate, not by a numeric score @implemented

# gameplay

## input-and-motion
- pressing or holding either endpoint button launches a Pulse from that end whenever that side has no active Pulse @implemented
- a launched Pulse remains white while moving and deactivates after leaving the opposite end @implemented

## collisions
- two active Pulses collide when their opposing paths meet or cross @implemented
- a collision is a Hit exactly when its Collision Span overlaps the Target Zone @implemented
- a Hit runs the whole-strip green Hit Animation and then removes both Pulses @implemented
- a Miss that does not trigger a Progress Reset removes both Pulses and displays a three-pixel Miss Marker centered on the Collision Span for seven render frames @implemented

## progression
- a Hit clears the Miss Streak and randomly relocates the Target Zone; while above minimum size, it also shrinks the Target Zone and increases its Breathing Rate @implemented
- a Miss increments the Miss Streak @implemented
- the third consecutive Miss triggers a Progress Reset that flashes the entire strip red, restores the Target Zone's configured initial size and Breathing Rate, randomly relocates it, and clears the Miss Streak @implemented

## target-zone
- the configured Target Zone size equals the number of yellow pixels it occupies @implemented
